# CE-EP-001-IMP-001 — Audience Engagement Phase 1 VS Code Implementation Specification

## Status

Approved for Implementation

---

# Purpose

Implement the Audience Engagement Phase 1 capability as defined by CE-EP-001.

Implementation shall follow the existing BTA architectural standards while establishing the first Platform Interaction Capability.

This implementation shall integrate with HubSpot CRM using the existing Personal Access Key.

---

# Implementation Rules

Implement only what is described in this document.

Do not introduce additional features.

Do not redesign existing BTA functionality.

Do not implement PostgreSQL.

Do not implement Identity.

Do not implement Marketing Automation.

Do not implement Analytics.

Do not implement ETL.

Do not implement OAuth.

Do not implement Authentication.

Do not implement Authorization.

---

# Architectural Goal

Implement a complete end-to-end workflow:

Visitor

↓

Stay Connected

↓

Frontend Validation

↓

Backend Route

↓

Engagement Service

↓

HubSpot Contact API

↓

HubSpot Contact Created

↓

Confirmation Screen

---

# Required Folder Structure

Create frontend Audience Engagement capability.

Create backend Engagement Route.

Create backend Engagement Service.

Create shared Engagement Types.

Create HubSpot integration module if required.

Use existing BTA project conventions.

---

# Frontend Responsibilities

Implement reusable StayConnectedCard component.

Collect:

• Name

• Email

• Consent

Perform client-side validation.

Submit to backend Engagement Route.

Display success confirmation.

Display friendly error message if submission fails.

No CRM logic shall exist in the frontend.

---

# Backend Responsibilities

Create Engagement Route.

Receive submission.

Validate request.

Create HubSpot contact.

Return success.

Return meaningful error when required.

No presentation logic shall exist within backend services.

---

# Environment Variables

Use environment variables only.

Do not hardcode credentials.

Support:

HUBSPOT_ACCESS_TOKEN

No credentials shall be committed to source control.

---

# HubSpot Contact

Initial fields:

First Name

Email

Consent

Source

Submitted Timestamp

Additional fields may be added in future versions.

---

# Source Identifier

Initial implementation:

BTA-STAY-CONNECTED

This value shall remain configurable.

---

# UI Placement

Initially place the component after Reflection.

This placement is temporary.

Implementation shall remain independent of page layout.

The component must be movable without code changes.

---

# Existing Code

Follow the same architectural layering used by the existing Donation capability.

Reuse architectural structure only.

Do not copy Donation implementation.

Do not duplicate Donation business logic.

---

# Testing

Validate:

✓ Component renders.

✓ Validation functions.

✓ Backend route reachable.

✓ HubSpot authentication successful.

✓ Contact created in HubSpot.

✓ Confirmation displayed.

✓ Errors handled gracefully.

---

# Acceptance Criteria

Implementation is complete only when:

✓ Contact successfully appears in HubSpot.

✓ User receives confirmation.

✓ No application regressions occur.

✓ No existing BTA functionality is modified.

✓ Implementation follows CE-EP-001.

---

